int x = 10;
int y = 13;
int z = 22;
auto test_tup = std::make_tuple(x, y, z);
std::cout << "Sum3(" << x << "," << y << "," << z << ") = "
    << emp::ApplyTuple(Sum3, test_tup) << std::endl;
std::cout << "Prod3(" << x << "," << y << "," << z << ") = "
```

Your task is to implement the `ApplyTuple` function and define the `Sum3` and `Prod3` functions to calculate the sum and product of the three input arguments, respectively.

Write a C++ program that includes the implementation of the `ApplyTuple` function and the `Sum3` and `Prod3` functions, and demonstrates the usage of `ApplyTuple` with the given test tuple.

### Solution:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <tuple>

namespace emp {
    // Function to apply a tuple of arguments to a given function and return the result
    template <typename Func, typename Tuple, std::size_t... I>
    decltype(auto) ApplyTupleHelper(Func&& func, Tuple&& args, std::index_sequence<I...>) {
        return std::forward<Func>(func)(std::get<I>(std::forward<Tuple>(args))...);
    }

    template <typename Func, typename... Args>
    decltype(auto) ApplyTuple(Func&& func, const std::tuple<Args...>& args) {
        return ApplyTupleHelper(std::forward<Func>(func), args, std::index_sequence_for<Args...>{});
    }
}

// Function to calculate the sum of three input arguments
int Sum3(int a, int b, int c) {
    return a + b + c;
}

// Function to calculate the product of three input arguments
int Prod3(int a, int b, int c) {
    return a * b * c;
}

int main() {
    std::cout << "\nApplyTuple results...:\n";
    int x = 10;
    int y = 13;
    int z = 22;
    auto test_tup = std::make_tuple(x, y, z);
    std::cout << "Sum3(" << x << "," << y << "," << z << ") = "
        << emp::ApplyTuple(Sum3, test_tup) << std::endl;
    std::cout << "Prod3(" << x << "," << y << "," << z << ") = "
        << emp::ApplyTuple(Prod3, test_tup) << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

In this solution, the `ApplyTuple` function is implemented using template metaprogramming to apply a tuple of arguments to a given function. The `ApplyTupleHelper` function is used to unpack the tuple and apply the arguments to the function. The `Sum3` and `Prod3` functions are defined to calculate the sum and product of the three input arguments, respectively. The `main` function demonstrates the usage of `ApplyTuple` with the given test tuple, showing the results of applying the `Sum3` and `Prod3` functions to the tuple.

