You are tasked with implementing a function to convert a SHA-256 hash to a Content Identifier (CID) using the multihash format. The multihash format is a self-describing hash format that includes a hash function code, the length of the hash, and the hash value itself. The CID is a unique identifier used in content-addressable systems like IPFS (InterPlanetary File System).

